From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:20:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(kanban): incomplete model output ends a worker run as
 a named failure

When a response stays truncated (finish_reason=length) after the bounded
recovery, run_conversation returns directly without finalize_turn. The
partial tool call is never executed, but a kanban worker then exits 0 and
the dispatcher records a protocol violation whose retry guidance tells the
next worker the prior run may already have done the work. Mark each
incomplete-output return with a machine-readable incomplete_output kind and
record it from AIAgent.run_conversation as a failed run (STOP
MODEL_OUTPUT_INCOMPLETE ...) through _record_task_failure, like the
iteration-budget and guardrail-halt paths.

The shared recorder is gated on is_dispatcher_owned_worker_context(), so a
delegated child or in-process cron job can no longer close the worker's
task; the guardrail-halt recorder (previous patch) now goes through it.
---
 agent/conversation_loop.py |  14 ++++-
 agent/turn_finalizer.py    | 110 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 run_agent.py               |  10 ++++
 3 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

